CREATED:20251219T211311Z
DESCRIPTION:<div dir="auto">C-House Environmental Racism Info Session<div d
 ir="auto"><div dir="auto">Hello and thank you for your interest in living i
 n the <a href="https://www.macalester.edu/lscsj/culturalhouse/"><u>Cultural
  House</u></a> and being part of next year's community! Participation in th
 e experiential learning and community components are mandatory elements of 
 being a C-House 2026-27 resident. It is open to rising Sophomores\, Juniors
 \, and Seniors.<br><br>For the 2026-27 academic year\, the Cultural House L
 iving Learning Community will focus on Environmental Racism. Residents will
  engage in experiential learning opportunities to explore environmental jus
 tice projects and community organizing efforts led by local communities thr
 oughout the Twin Cities. <br><br><br><br>Attending an info session is stron
 gly encouraged. Info sessions will be hosted by LSC staff in the Flemming R
 oom (LSC event space on the first floor of Kagin) and include lunch on: <br
 ><br>Thursday\, January 29\, 2026 @ 12 - 1pm (CST)<br>Tuesday\, February 3\
 , 2026 @ 12 - 1pm (CST)<br><br>If you have any questions or are unable to a
 ttend any of the provided sessions\, please reach out to the <a href="https
 ://www.macalester.edu/lscsj/"><u>Lealtad-Suzuki Center for Social Justice</
 u></a> through email at <a href="http://lsc@macalester.edu/"><u>lsc@macales
 ter.edu</u></a> or directly to Sam Taitel at <a href="http://staitel@macale
 ster.edu/"><u>staitel@macalester.edu</u></a>.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260202T173755Z
LOCATION:Flemming Room
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:C-House Info Session - Flemming Room
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
